<title>JAPAN: Nissho Iwai to loan Brazil's Petrobras 17 bln yen.</title>
<headline>Nissho Iwai to loan Brazil's Petrobras 17 bln yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissho Iwai Corp said on Wednesday it would loan Brazilian state oil firm Petrobras about 17 billion yen to construct a residue fluid catalytic cracking unit.</p>
<p>The unit, with capacity of 20,000 barrels per day (bpd), will be built at Petrobras's 40,000 bpd Recap refinery in Sao Paulo, a Nissho Iwai spokesman said.</p>
<p>A tender will be issued in January 1997 for equipment and contracting work, he said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Energy Desk +813-5473-3708</p>
